{"body":"[A10] Newly discovered during the #437 correction for draft PR #515. This is separate from optional R238 F3 in #495. Recording it here does not resolve the regression or unblock #437.\n\n## Objective and observed evidence\n\nThe Contents walk must not authorize labels for headings absent from the rendered page. A fresh synthetic GitHub render contains no heading elements for this input:\n\n```text\n- item\n\n  text\n<span>\n<!--\n\n## Old\n</span>\n\n## Real\n```\n\nThe walk at dev `88e9276b2a220c716f64a843f7e1eb8f9265e896` lists no headings. Both #437's first head `65df1df50a80cd5f540a93d8f0cfabc97da3da75` and local correction `b5e6c23e1b9802b5cacbc62db212064d7e429862` list Old and Real. Twelve measured variants cover first/resumed paragraphs, tag columns zero/one, and opening/closing/attribute forms. Six resumed variants regress from the original base; six first-paragraph counterparts are already wrong there. These are recorded mismatches, not passing controls.\n\n[Original public observation](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/437#issuecomment-5778541581), [immutable factual packet](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/tree/9f5e84cee18b20ed7cb0b2c8cc5cd620370adc0d/review-evidence/437-r1/correction-a172): `additional-observation.md`, `exploratory-unclosed-comments.json`, `three-revision-probes.json` and reproduction scripts.\n\n## Authority and entry points\n\n- #437's CommonMark/GFM authority and frozen acceptance contract.\n- CONTRIBUTING section 6.1, REQUIREMENTS REQ-VER-04, AGENTS sections 4/6/7.\n- `scripts/gen_toc.py` raw HTML/item-paragraph state and `scripts/check_em_dash.py` navigation provenance consumer.\n- #413's declared HTML limits and #495's explicitly optional R238 F3, which must not absorb a new regression by paperwork.\n\n## Scope and unresolved decision\n\nDetermine the rendering contract at the raw HTML/unclosed-comment boundary, including whether the difference comes from Markdown block parsing or HTML handling by the actual renderer. Publish a bounded fix scope and its effect on #437 before implementation. The six introduced mismatches remain an open merge condition for #437 pending an independent reviewer disposition; this issue is not a waiver. The pre-existing counterparts keep their own attribution.\n\nOut of scope: changing the exemption policy, provenance authority, unrelated container-heading omissions, or widening budgets to obtain a pass.\n\n## Acceptance and validation\n\n1. Preserve the twelve exact synthetic requests/responses and compare baseline, #437 source and corrected behavior with explicit commit identities.\n2. Resolve each in-scope mismatch against the selected renderer contract, with positive closed-comment and boundary controls in both navigation and real-Git em-dash consumers.\n3. A narrow mutation must fail for this property; unrelated case failures do not establish detection.\n4. Preserve #437's frozen acceptance criteria, existing controls and tracked-page classifications, or publish a reasoned contract change before work.\n5. Focused documentation/selftests, the complete required validation bar, independent review with all five lenses, and current-candidate/post-merge checks pass before any merge claiming resolution.\n\n## Dependencies and roles\n\nBacklog pending the rendering/scope decision. Conflicts with the active #437 parser lane; do not open a second editing lane against those files. Manager A10; implementation executor unassigned; independent reviewer assignment precedes implementation. R237/R238 remain the owners of their existing #437 findings and labels. This task does not clear R237 F2's separate historical-fixture evidence gap.\n","state":"OPEN","title":"[Docs] Resolve headings invented after unclosed comments inside raw HTML"}
